{"entryId":"1990","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1990:1","sourceSha256":"f58908781aa8893dc0af3766fd11d8d081e9126b7f61364dbc6385299bd1d08b","englishSha256":"994fa7b4828cdb8b2547f6639515c16bf40fb7ba6124ba056588697a2481b72c","citations":[{"id":"1990:1:link-01","he":[29,48],"en":[32,66],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Makhshirin_1.3"},"reference":"Mishnah Makhshirin 1:3","assessment":"The Mishnah records Rabbi Yehoshua’s transmission from Abba Yose Chali Kufri of Tivon in the discussion of liquids.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Makhshirin 1:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Makhshirin_1.3"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1990:1:link-02","he":[100,119],"en":[189,227],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Chet_167"},"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Chet 167","assessment":"The Arukh’s entry is חליקופרי and explains it as a name epithet, while Tivon is a named place.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Chet 167","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Chet_167"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"}]},{"id":"1990:1:link-03","he":[121,167],"en":[229,303],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rambam_on_Mishnah_Makhshirin_1.3.2"},"reference":"Rambam on Mishnah Makhshirin 1:3:2","assessment":"Maimonides’ Mishnah commentary treats Chali Kufri as an epithet and Tivon as a place. Preserve Heilprin’s distinct Chalifkori form.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rambam on Mishnah Makhshirin 1:3:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rambam_on_Mishnah_Makhshirin_1.3.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rambam on Mishnah Makhshirin 1:3:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rambam_on_Mishnah_Makhshirin_1.3.3"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1990:1:link-04","he":[169,194],"en":[305,338],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_323.3"},"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 323:3","assessment":"The Sifrei’s teaching on Deuteronomy 32:30 has Chanina of Tiv’in, while Yalkut’s parallel gives Chananya of Kefar Tivon. The different figure remains distinct from Abba Yose.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 323:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_323.3"},"witness":"Sefaria Vocalized Edition"},{"reference":"Yalkut Shimoni on Torah 946:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yalkut_Shimoni_on_Torah_946.4"},"witness":"Torat Emet"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The Mishnah records Rabbi Yehoshua’s transmission from Abba Yose Chali Kufri of Tivon in the discussion of liquids.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Arukh’s entry is חליקופרי and explains it as a name epithet, while Tivon is a named place.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Maimonides’ Mishnah commentary treats Chali Kufri as an epithet and Tivon as a place. Preserve Heilprin’s distinct Chalifkori form.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Sifrei’s teaching on Deuteronomy 32:30 has Chanina of Tiv’in, while Yalkut’s parallel gives Chananya of Kefar Tivon. The different figure remains distinct from Abba Yose.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Makhshirin 1:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Makhshirin_1.3"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Chet 167","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Chet_167"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"},{"reference":"Rambam on Mishnah Makhshirin 1:3:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rambam_on_Mishnah_Makhshirin_1.3.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rambam on Mishnah Makhshirin 1:3:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rambam_on_Mishnah_Makhshirin_1.3.3"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 323:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_323.3"},"witness":"Sefaria Vocalized Edition"},{"reference":"Yalkut Shimoni on Torah 946:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Y